        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What to Expect After a Utah Windstorm"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Immediate Tarping: If shingles have blown off or the roof is actively leaking, call for emergency tarping or board-up services to prevent interior water damage.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Check Vulnerable Areas: High canyon winds in Utah frequently target ridge caps, loose flashing around chimneys and vents, and soffits/fascia rather than just flat shingle fields. Refer to the 4 Seasons Restoration Homeowner Guide for a full post-storm checklist.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "4 Seasons Restoration Homeowner Guide",
                "link": "https://www.4seasonsrestoration.com/what-to-do-after-storm-and-wind-damage-to-your-utah-home-a-complete-homeowners-guide/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insurance Documentation: Reputable local roofers will walk the roof with a camera, take detailed line-item photos of lifted or missing shingles, and help coordinate directly with your insurance adjuster. For broad emergency services across the state, consider Utah Disaster Restoration Services .",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
